Feature request
===============

Feature name:

AgentCore Toolkit Target Entra Group Protection

Background
----------

The Guardian AI Control Plane has the following hierarchy:

Organization
  -> Project
      -> Agent

Users can create agents within a project.

We are using AWS AgentCore Harness v2 for agent runtime/deployment.

An Agent can be assigned one or more Toolkits.

A Toolkit is our Control Plane abstraction for an AWS AgentCore Gateway.

A Toolkit / AgentCore Gateway can contain multiple targets.

Feature behavior
----------------

When a user creates or configures a target inside a Toolkit / AgentCore Gateway,
the user must be able to select the Microsoft Entra group that should be associated
with/protect access to that target.

Conceptually:

Project
  -> Agent
      -> Toolkit
          -> AgentCore Gateway
              -> Target
                  -> selected Entra Group

The user creating the Toolkit target selects an approved Entra group.

The Control Plane must retain that selected Entra group configuration as part of
the target configuration.

When the AgentCore Harness / Toolkit infrastructure is provisioned or updated,
the platform must use the saved identity/access configuration when configuring
the AgentCore target and its security integration.

Important intent-level requirement:

The Intent should capture WHAT capability we are introducing and WHY.

Do not prematurely decide HOW Entra authentication/authorization is technically
implemented inside AgentCore.

For example, do not assume in intent.md:
- whether an Entra App Registration is created per Gateway or per Target
- whether group information becomes a token claim, policy, scope, or another
  AgentCore authorization configuration
- the exact AWS resource implementation
- the exact database schema

Those are Design-stage questions.

Business/platform objective
---------------------------

Agent teams should not have to manually configure identity protection for Toolkit
targets outside the Control Plane.

The Control Plane should provide a governed way to associate an approved Entra
group with a Toolkit target and carry that identity configuration into the managed
AgentCore deployment lifecycle.

Expected capabilities
---------------------

At a high level, the feature should support:

1. A user creating/configuring a Toolkit target can select an approved Entra group.

2. The selected group is stored as part of the Control Plane-managed target
   configuration.

3. The configuration remains associated with the correct:
   - Organization
   - Project
   - Toolkit
   - Gateway
   - Target

4. The selected identity configuration is supplied to the AgentCore deployment /
   update workflow.

5. Existing authorization and ownership boundaries must be respected.

6. The configuration should be available for lifecycle operations such as:
   - create
   - update
   - redeploy
   - future environment promotion

7. The feature should maintain sufficient auditability to determine which Entra
   group was selected for a target and when the configuration changed.

